    bio: 'With a PhD in Educational Psychology from Cambridge University and 12 years of experience in game design, Emma leads our quiz creation team with unparalleled expertise. Her innovative approach combines cognitive science with entertainment, ensuring every puzzle challenges your mind while keeping you engaged.',
    longBio: 'Dr. Emma Richardson\'s journey into quiz design began during her doctoral research on gamification in education. She discovered that well-crafted puzzles could improve memory retention by up to 340% compared to traditional learning methods. This revelation sparked her passion for creating brain games that are both educational and addictive.\n\nBefore joining LogicLeague, Emma worked as Lead Game Designer at two major educational technology companies, where she pioneered adaptive difficulty algorithms that personalize quiz experiences. Her work has been featured in journals like "Cognitive Science Today" and "Digital Learning Review."\n\nEmma has designed over 5,000 quizzes that have been played by millions worldwide. Her specialty lies in logic puzzles and trivia that make complex subjects accessible and fun. When she\'s not crafting the perfect question, you\'ll find her competing in pub quiz championships across Europe.',
    expertise: ['Logic Puzzle Design', 'Educational Gaming', 'Cognitive Science', 'Adaptive Difficulty Systems', 'Gamification Theory'],
